{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, I looked into it. Your mailbox is 99.4% full, about 49.7 GB of a 50 GB limit, and that's why Outlook keeps warning you and some emails won't send. To free up space: 1) Empty your Deleted Items and Junk Email folders. 2) Sort your Inbox and Sent Items by size, then delete large emails you don't need or save their attachments to OneDrive and delete the emails. 3) If you need to keep old mail, turn on Online Archive and move anything older than a year into it. The mailbox can take up to an hour to show the new size. After that, check whether the warning is gone and your emails send. If it's still over 95% after cleanup and your work needs more space, reply here and we'll look at a larger mailbox, which needs your manager's approval.",
  "internal_note": "Looked up user_id 9 (Mei Chen, Operations). Mailbox is at 99.4% (50,890 of 51,200 MB). That explains the near-full warnings and the failed sends. Account is active with no lockouts. Gave her the KB-010 cleanup steps: empty Deleted Items and Junk, delete or move large attachments to OneDrive, turn on Online Archive for mail older than a year. No technician actions requested. If she's still over 95% after cleanup and needs a bigger quota, escalate to Tier 2 with manager approval as KB-010 says.",
